.TH HSH 1 "2026-05-12" "simple_shell"

.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple UNIX command line interpreter written in C.

The shell displays a prompt and waits for the user to enter a command.
Commands are executed using
.BR execve (2).

The shell supports both interactive and noninteractive modes.

.PP
The shell can:
.IP \[bu] 2
Display a prompt and read user input.
.IP \[bu] 2
Execute commands with arguments.
.IP \[bu] 2
Search for executable files using the
.B PATH
environment variable.
.IP \[bu] 2
Handle errors.
.IP \[bu] 2
Handle the end-of-file condition
.RB ( Ctrl\-D ).
.IP \[bu] 2
Execute the built-in commands
.B exit
and
.B env.

.SS Command execution
When a command is entered, the shell:
.IP (1) 3
Reads the input line.
.IP (2) 3
Parses the command into tokens.
.IP (3) 3
Searches for the command in
.B PATH.
.IP (4) 3
Creates a child process using
.BR fork (2).
.IP (5) 3
Executes the command using
.BR execve (2).
.IP (6) 3
Waits for the child process to terminate using
.BR wait (2).

.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.

.TP
.B env
Print the current environment variables.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATH
A colon-separated list of directories used to locate executable programs.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (command not found or execution failure).

.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive mode:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
$ ./hsh
$ ls
$ main.c shell.c
$ env
$ exit
.EE
.in

Noninteractive mode:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
$ main.c shell.c
.EE
.in

.SH BUGS
The shell does not support pipes, redirections, command chaining,
or special characters.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR execve (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR wait (2)
